TRANSITION PHASE: CONTACT -> FOOTER (The Hard Snap)

Vibe: Breaking the fourth wall. A hard system interrupt. Waking up from
the simulation.
Goal: Create a jarring, instantly memorable psychological loop ("Deja Vu")
that proves your UI mastery by abruptly killing the chaotic physics and
returning to a highly disciplined, static grid.

SCROLL MECHANICS (The Threshold)

This transition uses standard vertical scrolling, but relies on a strict
Intersection Observer threshold to trigger the state change.

The Boundary: There is no gradient or fade between the pitch-black Cave
and the Footer. They are separated by a razor-sharp, 1px solid line
using #1E293B (Light Slate).

The Trigger Point: The transition event fires the exact millisecond the
Footer's top boundary enters the viewport (0% threshold).

STAGE 1: THE COMMAND PROMPT (Visual Cue)

As the user scrolls down past the bottom of the cave, the first thing
they see crossing the 1px boundary line is the override code.

Text: > system.override(tototofu); // take off headset

Typography: Space Grotesk, #94A3B8.

Placement: Sitting directly on the top edge of the Footer container.
It acts as the physical "tripwire" for the transition.

STAGE 2: THE HARD SNAP (Execution)

The moment the tripwire is crossed, the simulation is violently terminated.

Color Reversion: The #000000 (Pitch Black) or Amber firelight of the
Contact section instantly vanishes. The background below the line is pure
#0F172A (Deep Matte Slate), exactly matching the Hero section.

Canvas Destruction:

Any remaining WebGL contexts, particle emitters, or active shaders from
the Water and Earth sections are explicitly unmounted/destroyed.

There must be absolutely ZERO lingering animations, fading opacities, or
easing curves. It is a 0-millisecond binary cut.

Lighting Reset: If the user had ignited the torch in the cave, scrolling
past the tripwire extinguishes it instantly. If they scroll back up, the
cave is pitch black again (the simulation has reset).

STAGE 3: THE DEJA VU (Psychological Loop)

The user is now fully in the Footer, realizing the journey has looped.

Visual Echo: The user immediately recognizes the exact same 4-column UI
grid structure, the same Space Grotesk typography, and the identical
color palette from the very first section (Hero).

The Artifact: The t.tofu logo, which was ancient stone a few pixels ago,
is rendered here as a flat, pristine, single-color SVG (#1E293B), proving
they have left the "physical" world and returned to the "digital" UI layer.

TECHNICAL UX & PERFORMANCE NOTES

React Cleanup: This transition acts as your garbage collector. Bind an
IntersectionObserver to the Footer component. When isIntersecting is true,
dispatch a global state (e.g., setSimulationActive(false)) that immediately
unmounts the heavy Canvas components sitting in the DOM above it. This ensures
that when the recruiter reaches the bottom of the page to click your Resume or
GitHub links, the website is running at an ultra-lightweight 60fps with zero
background GPU usage.

CSS Warning: Triple-check that there are no transition: background-color 0.5s
rules applied globally to the <body> or <main> wrapper, as that would ruin
the instant "snap" effect.